  "body": "## Status\n\nResearch construction; no new \u03ba and no selected-frontier change.\n\n## Result\n\nFor the pinned order-four, five-child interface, this package checks two independent 24-coordinate source banks `X,Y` with arbitrary dirty `D` and a restored workspace. The exact map is `D -> D + \u03a3_{i=0..4} R_i X + \u03a3_{i=5..9} R_i Y`.\n\nThe phase-indexed child type is `C_(i,t)(D,W)=(D+Q^(-t)R_i W, P W)`, with `Q^(-t)R_iP^t=R_i`. At the fixed 5|5 split, the source-bank handoff is `W += P^3(Y-X)`, charged at 48 ADDs. Exhaustive recurrence checks cover all `4^5=1,024` and `4^10=1,048,576` phase paths, and both complete maps replay on all 80 basis columns.\n\nThe typed calls cost 1,696 primitives separately and 1,552 jointly (144 saved; 288 fewer reads). A distinct unchanged-reader control costs 2,016 separately and 1,952 jointly (64 saved). Five negative controls reject omitted or mistyped handoff, omitted restoration, and omitted literal inverse. These are exact costs in the declared signed-ADD word model; supplier routing, tape/hosting, fixed-precision admission, and transfer into the selected recursive supplier remain unproved.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n```sh\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/z4-distinct-source-seed55\n```\n\nExpected result includes:\n\n```text\nPASS_Z4_DISTINCT_SOURCE_PHASE_TYPED_ECHO g5=60 g10=48 separate=1696 joint=1552 saved=144 reads_saved=288 paths=1024+1048576 basis=80 controls=5\nPASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE research/z4-distinct-source-seed55 outcome=completed\n```\n\n## Pins and overlap\n\nAssignment base: `4040a0f46d67b41c36a472a7cd4af791fd4c36cc`. Publication parent: current `main` at `ef5f39403610d231a0c27e8a6b4f08c10209bcd6`. The exact predecessor heads and vendored snapshots for PR #1391 (`6ce8017e4c27c8b220b6c3a27a53bb18f138212a`) and PR #1410 (`5b1c00b9f2770aabaa0085539405757f7818a14a`) are pinned in `SOURCES.json` and `NOTICE.md`. Selected context remains #1094, \u03ba=`836330098538459/500000000000000000`.\n\nAdjacent work is credited and distinguished in the README: PR #1158's four-source Hadamard census; PR #1438 and Discussion #1412's two-root transfers; PR #1439's `BCu` correction for a persistent connector under source mutation; and PR #1442's chronological delivery-cut optimum. This package claims no priority over those models.\n\nPrepared by **Cinna Davis** with substantial **OpenAI Codex assistance** in derivation, implementation, exact verification, source pinning, and writing. No independent human review or proof-assistant formalization is claimed. Apache-2.0.\n",
